# KNOWN GAP — D26 shift-fallible Route B (Result-capture) is not yet lowered
# to Result construction. The Rust check-lane REJECTS this shape today with
# `E_ShiftFallibleRouteBNotYetImplemented` (see
# `tests/fixtures/c1_d26_shift_capture_rejects.gg` for the currently-live
# reject), so the SIGSEGV miscompile that used to happen at this shape is
# now blocked by the check-lane. This fixture pins the INTENDED behavior for
# when the follow-up lands.
#
# INTENDED: `gg check` accepts; `gg build` compiles; run prints `16`.
# `4 <<! 2 = 16` → `Result[int, ArithError].Ok(16)` at the capture destination;
# the match's Ok arm fires.
#
# CURRENT: `gg check` rejects with `E_ShiftFallibleRouteBNotYetImplemented`
# (Core #10 same-round compliance for the Core #8 miscompile — the SIGSEGV
# was the specific defect the check reject retires). Route A (throws-
# propagate via auto-infer) already works for shift-fallible via the base-op
# trap-on-oob path — see `c1_d26_shift_shl_ok.gg`.
#
# FIX SHAPE: extend the `FaultableBinOp` LIR variant to accept Shl/Shr with a
# new `FaultOp::ShlOverflow`/`ShrOverflow` category (a shift amount >= operand
# width is the fault trigger), then extend `lower_fallible_arith_binop`'s
# `base_op` match in `src/ir/lowering/exprs/operators.rs` to route the 2
# shift-fallible variants through the same Route-A / Route-B machinery the 5
# arith fallible ops use. When it lands, the check-lane reject retires and
# this fixture graduates to `tests/fixtures/c1_d26_shift_capture_shl_ok.gg`
# (a positive Route-B test); a sibling `_overflow.gg` fixture then covers
# the overflow-branch construction of `Error(ArithError.Overflow)`.
#
# Filed at TODO.md "Semantics / reference-grade rejection > High" as the
# "D26 shift-fallible Route B lowering gap" entry. Un-ignore
# `c1_d26_shift_capture_type_mismatch_intended` in `tests/integration.rs`
# when the follow-up lands and this fixture graduates.
void main():
    int a = 4
    int b = 2
    Result[int, ArithError] r = a <<! b
    match r:
        case Ok(v): print(v)
        case Error(e): print(-1)
